 "strategy": {
  "summary": "Trade stock index futures in the day's direction into the close. Baltussen, Da, Lammers & Martens (JFE 2021) find across 60+ futures (1974\u20132020) that the move from the previous close to 30 minutes before today's close predicts the last half hour: for equity index futures, going long if the day is up and short if it is down earned a Sharpe of 1.7 before costs. They tie it to dealers and leveraged ETFs hedging in the day's direction near the close. Replications after 2013 find the plain version near zero, but still working on days dealers are short gamma; the filters here are price-based stand-ins for those days.",
  "formula": "sign(price now \u00f7 reference \u2212 1): long if up, short if down, from the entry time to the exit time",
  "rules": [
   {
    "label": "Signal",
    "text": "The day's move so far: the previous session's last close to the minute before the entry (the paper's), today's 09:30 open to the same minute (no overnight gap), or the previous close to 10:00 (the first half hour only). Optionally it must have the same sign as the first-half-hour move."
   },
   {
    "label": "Filter",
    "text": "None; the move bigger than 0.5\u03c3 or 1\u03c3 of the same signal over the previous 20 days; only when 20-day volatility is above its 120-day median; or only down days (shorts only)."
   },
   {
    "label": "Enter",
    "text": "At 15:00, 15:30, 15:45 or 15:50 ET, at that minute's open, long if the signal is up and short if down."
   },
   {
    "label": "Exit",
    "text": "At 15:50 or 16:00 ET, at the close of the minute before (16:00 = the last regular-session bar). Optional stop 0.1%, 0.2% or 0.4% against the entry price, live during the trade. Early-close days are not traded."
   },
   {
    "label": "Size",
    "text": "One position at a time, never held overnight. As many whole ES contracts as the account covers at full contract value (no leverage), starting from $1,000,000."
   }
  ],
  "axes": [
